### F2 — Refusal redesign (Validation-first, entire source scan, 3 condition classes)
- [`libs/migrate/src/migrate/inventory.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp1/libs/migrate/src/migrate/inventory.py#L271-L439):
  - Validates batch envelope and batch rows **first** (matching `engine/arrival_body.py:229-238` ordering) before evaluating observer conditions; invalid rows/types land cleanly in `codec_invalid_lines`.
  - Scans the entire source before raising any exception, accumulating into three distinct classes: `codec_invalid_lines`, `mixed_observer_lines`, and `absent_observer_lines`.
  - A batch line exhibiting both mixed and absent aspects (e.g. `alice`, `bob`, and 1 observerless row) is reported once under `mixed_observer_lines` with present observers and absent-row count visible.
  - Multi-class errors raise [`MigrationRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp1/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L74-L146) containing all offending lines across all three classes without preemption.
- [`libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp1/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L23-L245):
  - Expanded [`MigrationRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp1/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L74-L146) structured fields to carry `codec_invalid_lines`, `mixed_observer_lines`, and `absent_observer_lines` distinctly.
  - Formatted refusal message to render each class in its own labeled section, maintaining advisory prose in the message only.
- [`libs/migrate/tests/_fixtures.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp1/libs/migrate/tests/_fixtures.py#L366-L566): Added fixture builders `build_combined_defects_jsonl`, `build_both_aspects_batch_jsonl`, and `build_type_error_batch_jsonl`.
